{"id":"pathros","name":"Pathros","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:pathros"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Pathros","text":"The name generally given to Upper Egypt (the Thebaid of the Greeks), as distinguished from Matsor, or Lower Egypt (Isa. 11:11; Jer. 44:1, 15; Ezek. 30:14), the two forming Mizraim. After the destruction of Jerusalem by Nebuchadnezzar, colonies of Jews settled “in the country of Pathros” and other parts of Egypt."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H6624","lemma":"פַּתְרוֹס","xlit":"Pathrôwç","gloss":"Pathros, a part of Egypt","kjv":"Pathros","count":5,"share":1},{"strong":"H3414","lemma":"יִרְמְיָה","xlit":"Yirmᵉyâh","gloss":"Jirmejah, the name of eight or nine Israelites","kjv":"Jeremiah","count":2,"share":0.4}],"verses":["Isa.11.11","Jer.44.1","Jer.44.15","Ezek.29.14","Ezek.30.14"],"related":[{"id":"azriel","type":"lexical","strong":"H3414","why":"both lead with יִרְמְיָה (H3414)"},{"id":"ebed-melech","type":"lexical","strong":"H3414","why":"both lead with יִרְמְיָה (H3414)"},{"id":"jehucal","type":"lexical","strong":"H3414","why":"both lead with יִרְמְיָה (H3414)"},{"id":"jeremiah","type":"lexical","strong":"H3414","why":"both lead with יִרְמְיָה (H3414)"},{"id":"shelemiah","type":"lexical","strong":"H3414","why":"both lead with יִרְמְיָה (H3414)"}],"works":[]}
